# RFC Code — deploy env (T16). Copy to deploy/.env and edit, or export these
# inline before `docker compose up`. See deploy/README.md for the full guide.

# --- Host paths (persistent state) ------------------------------------------

# Parent directory of every project you want browsable in the UI (HUB-07 AC1).
#PROJECTS_ROOT=/srv/rfc-code/projects

# Holds the SQLite DB and per-profile credential dirs — the only stateful
# thing in the whole deploy. Back this up.
#DATA_ROOT=/srv/rfc-code/data

# --- Network publish ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Default (below, commented): publish directly on intel's own tailnet
# interface. The service is reachable at http://intel:7789 (or
# http://100.70.101.109:7789) from any device on the tailnet, and from
# nowhere else — the public internet and the LAN never get a listener for
# this port (HUB-01 AC2). No `tailscale serve` needed for this mode.
#
#BIND_IP=100.70.101.109
#PORT=7789
#
# Alternative: keep the raw HTTP port off the tailnet entirely and front it
# with `tailscale serve` for HTTPS instead (needed if you want the PWA /
# service worker to work — browsers require HTTPS for those). Set:
#   BIND_IP=127.0.0.1
#   PORT=7789
# then, after `docker compose up -d`, run on intel:
#   sudo tailscale serve --bg https+insecure://127.0.0.1:7789
# which publishes https://intel.<your-tailnet>.ts.net/ to the tailnet only.

# --- notify-hub webhook (T18, reserved) --------------------------------------
# Safe to leave unset until this channel is wired up.
#NOTIFY_URL=
#NOTIFY_TOKEN=
